Our team chose this technology because of the significant impact that cancer and other chronic and life-threatening illnesses have on society. Early detection is critical in improving treatment outcomes and can increase survival rates. AI allows medical professionals to identify potential health risks earlier, giving them more time to intervene and develop effective treatment plans before illnesses progress.
Additionally, AI can reduce the administrative burden placed on medical professionals, allowing them to dedicate more time and attention to their patients.

Our team wanted to explore how AI can improve patient outcomes, quality of life, and operational efficiency while also examining the ethical challenges associated with relying on technology that can directly impact a person's health and survival.
